# Scoped to `docker build -f Dockerfile.acat-api` (BuildKit picks up
# <dockerfile-name>.dockerignore automatically).
#
# Defense in depth, not the primary safety mechanism: Dockerfile.acat-api's own
# COPY lines are an explicit allowlist (requirements.txt, acat/__init__.py,
# acat/api/) and determine image content regardless of how this file resolves.
# This one only limits what gets uploaded to the build daemon from an otherwise
# huge, mixed-content repo root — internal planning docs, a resume, zip
# archives, z1-inbox/, humanaios-funding-pipeline/entitlement-navigator/'s
# gitignored private/ evidence boundary, none of it relevant to this build.
#
# Ignore everything, then re-allow exactly the three inputs Dockerfile.acat-api
# COPYs. The directory must be re-allowed both as itself and as `dir/**` —
# re-allowing only the latter does not surface the directory entry itself.
*
!requirements.txt
!acat/
!acat/__init__.py
!acat/api/
!acat/api/**
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
